        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Multiple Choice Questions"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "1. Data science is mainly concerned with:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Designing hardware",
              "(b) Extracting useful information from data",
              "(c) Writing only code",
              "(d) Creating websites"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "2. Data organised in rows and columns is called:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Unstructured data",
              "(b) Structured data",
              "(c) Raw data",
              "(d) Random data"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "3. An example of unstructured data is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Tables",
              "(b) Spreadsheets",
              "(c) Images and videos",
              "(d) Databases"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "4. Machine learning allows systems to:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Work without data",
              "(b) Learn from data and improve performance",
              "(c) Only store data",
              "(d) Replace databases"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "5. The type of machine learning that uses labelled data is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Unsupervised learning",
              "(b) Reinforcement learning",
              "(c) Supervised learning",
              "(d) Rule-based learning"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "6. The machine learning method that learns through rewards and penalties is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Supervised learning",
              "(b) Unsupervised learning",
              "(c) Reinforcement learning",
              "(d) Rule-based learning"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "7. Feature engineering is used to:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Delete data",
              "(b) Improve data for better model performance",
              "(c) Store data",
              "(d) Visualise data"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "8. The metric that measures the overall correctness of a model is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Precision",
              "(b) Recall",
              "(c) Accuracy",
              "(d) F1-score"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "9. Train-test split is used to:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Delete data",
              "(b) Divide data for training and testing",
              "(c) Store data",
              "(d) Visualise data"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "10. A commonly used tool for machine learning and data analysis is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) MS Word",
              "(b) Python",
              "(c) PowerPoint",
              "(d) Notepad"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Short Questions"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "What is data science?",
              "What are the two main types of data?",
              "What is the difference between structured and unstructured data?",
              "Name two common data collection methods.",
              "What is machine learning?",
              "What is supervised learning?",
              "What is the purpose of feature selection in machine learning?",
              "What does accuracy measure in a model?",
              "What is the difference between prediction and causality?",
              "Name any one tool used for machine learning."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Long Questions"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "Explain the concept of data science and discuss its importance in modern applications.",
              "Describe different types of data and explain various data sources and collection methods.",
              "Explain the concept of machine learning and describe its different mechanisms, including supervised, unsupervised, reinforcement, and rule-based learning.",
              "Discuss the applications of machine learning in healthcare, business, education, and daily life.",
              "Explain the steps involved in building a machine learning model, including feature selection, feature engineering, and train-test split.",
              "Describe model evaluation techniques and explain accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score.",
              "Explain validation in machine learning and discuss how models can be improved using parameter tuning.",
              "Discuss predictive modeling and causality, and explain the importance of model interpretation in real-world use cases."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
